    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2077767983204610498",
      "url": "https://x.com/georgeprobook/status/2077767983204610498",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/georgeprobook/status/2077767983204610498",
      "text": "Home services companies are getting bombarded with a stack of point solutions. One tool for voice. One for outbound. Another for webchat. They end up with five vendors and more overhead.\n\nThe problem is that none of them talk to each other, and customers notice every seam. Which is the opposite of the experience operators are turning to AI to build in the first place.\n\nSo we built around dispatch, the brain of the business that actually makes or breaks the customer experience.\n\n@Forbes covered why. Most AI vendors came to this space because it looked good on a spreadsheet. We came because we grew up in it.\n\nFull story in comments.",
